Package: phenoshot
Title: AI-Based Plant Image Analysis for Morphological Trait Measurement
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("JK", "Kim", , "kimjk@agronomy4future.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-9913-8768"))
Description: Provides an automated pipeline for plant phenotyping through image
    analysis. Uses AI-based background removal (Photoroom API) combined with
    OpenCV-based object detection to measure morphological traits including
    area, perimeter, length, and width of plant objects. Additional steps
    remove thin non-target structures such as grass weed leaves, exclude
    background enclosed between objects from the measured area, and correct the
    pixel-to-centimeter scale either from a detected ArUco marker or from the
    camera and canopy heights. Every run writes a parameter log for
    reproducibility. Supports JPG, PNG, and HEIC image formats. Designed for
    agronomic research applications such as leaf area estimation, canopy cover
    assessment, fruit morphology analysis, and seedling measurement.
